     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ 
 --> ../../conformance/PROV/PROV-4-arena-aggregate-wrong-field-bad.hir:8:36
   8 | fn bad(a: Arena, b: Arena, take x: Bytes in b) -> Ast in a {
     |                                    ^^^^^^^^^^ provided: placed `in b` by its declared type
 --> ../../conformance/PROV/PROV-4-arena-aggregate-wrong-field-bad.hir:9:3
   9 |   Ast(bytes: take x)
     |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required: the constructed field requires `in a`; every part must outlive `a`
  = help: 1. declare `x` `in a` (no cost; signature)
  = help: 2. declare the result `in b` (no cost; signature)
  = help: 3. declare `x` `in heap` (no cost; signature)
  = note: `unique x` and `copy x` keep the placement of `x` and do not help
